# PASS0 annotations, keyed by object or storage address (development file).
# [names]     $addr NAME group MEANING      variables (storage address)
# [fns]       $addr NAME PARAM MEANING      DEF FN (body address)
# [routines]  $addr TITLE                   comment on a routine's first line
# [lines]     $addr COMMENT                 comment on the line starting at addr
[names]
$60D3 A$   dialog  THE ANSWER TYPED AT A QUESTION
$60DD L$   dialog  THE LINE TYPED AT A FILE QUESTION, THEN THE DOS COMMAND THAT CHECKS THE FILE
$6090 YN   dialog  ANSWER TO A YES/NO QUESTION: 1 YES, 0 NO, 2 NOTHING TYPED (THE DEFAULT)
$60CC BD   dialog  1 IF THE ANSWER WAS NOT ACCEPTED (THE QUESTION IS ASKED AGAIN)
$60BD QN   dialog  WHICH QUESTION IS BEING ANSWERED; SELECTS WHERE THE SHARED CHECKS RETURN
$60D7 NM$  spec    FILE NAME PART OF A FILE SPECIFICATION
$60D5 SD$  spec    SLOT AND DRIVE PART OF A FILE SPECIFICATION (",S6,D1")
$6081 NS   spec    1 IF THE FILE SPECIFICATION HAS NO SLOT OR DRIVE PART
$6095 CF   spec    1 RIGHT AFTER A COMMA IN THE SLOT AND DRIVE PART (S OR D MAY FOLLOW)
$60AE HS   spec    1 IF THE SPECIFICATION GIVES A SLOT
$609F GS   spec    THE SLOT IT GIVES
$60A4 HD   spec    1 IF THE SPECIFICATION GIVES A DRIVE
$60C2 GD   spec    THE DRIVE IT GIVES
$608B SL   spec    SLOT OF THE BOOT DRIVE (DOS'S LAST SLOT USED, $AA6A)
$60B8 DR   spec    DRIVE OF THE BOOT DRIVE (DOS'S LAST DRIVE USED, $AA68)
$6086 AD   memory  AN ADDRESS: A DOS BYTE TO PATCH, OR THE ADDRESS ANSWERED
$60A9 DA   memory  DEFAULT LIBRARY ADDRESS (2051 = $0803)
$60D9 C$   memory  ONE CHARACTER OF A HEXADECIMAL ADDRESS
$609A PV   tables  NEW VALUE OF A DOS BYTE BEING PATCHED
$60C7 X    tables  A VALUE READ FROM A DATA TABLE
$60B3 I    tables  LOOP INDEX; ALSO A LENGTH
$60DB DE$  text    DOS DELETE COMMAND
[fns]
$4278 SA X  ADDRESS X AS IT IS STORED IN AN INTEGER (X-32767)
$4285 RA X  THE ADDRESS STORED AS X (X+32767)
$428F SW X  ADDRESS X AS A SIGNED WORD FOR POKE AND PEEK (X-65536 ABOVE 32767)
[routines]
$4206 PASS 0 OF THE COMPILER: PATCHES DOS, ASKS FOR THE SOURCE AND OBJECT FILES, THE MEMORY LAYOUT AND THE OPTIONS, LOADS THE CALL TABLE, THE OPERATOR TABLE AND THE MACHINE CODE AT $0377-$03CF, SETS UP THE COMMON BLOCK AND RUNS PASS 1. SET UP DOS AND THE STRINGS
$4489 TITLE AND THE SOURCE FILE QUESTION
$4541 THE SOURCE FILE'S NAME WAS CHECKED: IT MUST EXIST
$45A7 THE SOURCE FILE EXISTS; THE OBJECT FILE QUESTION, ITS DEFAULT THE SOURCE NAME (UP TO 26 CHARACTERS) + .OBJ
$466B THE OBJECT FILE'S NAME WAS CHECKED
$46A1 MEMORY USAGE: THE DEFAULT, OR THE THREE ADDRESSES
$47C3 THE LIBRARY ADDRESS WAS CHECKED
$48C0 THE PROGRAM ADDRESS WAS CHECKED
$494B THE VARIABLES ADDRESS WAS CHECKED; SHOW THE LAYOUT AND CONFIRM IT
$4A7A OPTIONS: THE DEFAULT, OR EACH OPTION IN TURN
$4F8F THE CALL TABLE: ADDRESSES OF THE LIBRARY AND ROM ROUTINES THE COMPILED CODE CALLS, BY INDEX (A POSITIVE ENTRY IS AN OFFSET FROM THE LIBRARY ADDRESS, A NEGATIVE ONE MINUS A ROM ADDRESS), STORED IN {SY}(150..285) FOR PASS 1
$509A THE OPERATOR TABLE (TOKEN, STACK PRIORITY, ARRIVING PRIORITY) IN {SY}(300..350) FOR PASS 1
$5219 THE MACHINE CODE AT $0377-$03CF
$5265 THE SYMBOL TABLE'S CHAIN HEADS AND THE ADDRESSES OF THE MACHINE CODE ROUTINES
$52E1 CREATE THE OBJECT FILE, EMPTY THE LINE NUMBER FILE, AND RUN PASS 1
$53D3 YES/NO ANSWER: {YN} = 1 YES, 0 NO, 2 RETURN ALONE; {BD} = 1 FOR ANYTHING ELSE
$5463 READ A LINE FROM THE KEYBOARD INTO {L$} (CONTROL-C STOPS)
$54BC SPLIT THE FILE SPECIFICATION IN {L$} INTO {NM$} (THE NAME, LEADING SPACES REMOVED, TRAILING SPACES CUT, AT MOST 30 CHARACTERS) AND {SD$} (",SN,DN", THE BOOT DRIVE'S SLOT OR DRIVE FILLED IN WHERE MISSING); {BD} = 1 IF IT IS NOT LEGAL
$5787 REPORT AN ILLEGAL FILE SPECIFICATION
$57B7 CONVERT THE ADDRESS IN {A$} (DECIMAL, OR HEXADECIMAL AFTER $) INTO {AD}; {BD} = 1 IF IT IS NOT FROM 0 TO 49151; THEN RETURN TO THE QUESTION {QN}
$59B8 CHECK AN ANSWER: A LINE {L$} THAT STARTS WITH CONTROL-D IS A DOS COMMAND (CATALOG, FOR EXAMPLE): IT IS RUN, AND THE QUESTION IS ASKED AGAIN ...
$59EF ... ENTRY: RUN THE DOS COMMAND IN {L$}; A FILE NOT FOUND OR OTHER DOS ERROR SETS {BD}; THEN RETURN TO THE QUESTION {QN}
[lines]
$422C NO ECHO OF DOS COMMANDS, INPUT OR OUTPUT
$424E THREE FILE BUFFERS: SOURCE, OBJECT, LINE NUMBER FILE
$426F KEEP THE PROGRAMS' STRINGS BELOW $9600, UNDER THE DOS BUFFERS
$429F SIX DOS PATCHES (ADDRESS, NEW BYTE, ORIGINAL BYTE) SO THAT DOS CAN READ THE TOKENIZED PROGRAM AS A TEXT FILE: $A633-$A635 BNE $A644 / JSR $A2FC BECOMES JMP $A644, SO A ZERO BYTE DOES NOT END THE DATA READ INTO THE INPUT LINE; $A649 AND #$7F BECOMES AND #$FF, SO TOKENS KEEP BIT 7; $A7C4 BECOMES RTS, SO THE FILE TYPE IS NOT CHECKED (THE APPLESOFT SOURCE FILE OPENS AS A TEXT FILE); $A96C $7F BECOMES $FF, SO THE B (BYTE POSITION) PARAMETER MAY GO UP TO 65535
$4304 THE ADDRESS, THE NEW BYTE AND THE ORIGINAL BYTE (KEPT TO UNDO THE PATCH)
$4328 PATCH DOS
$4334 THE ADDRESS, AS A SIGNED WORD, FOR PUTTING THE BYTE BACK AT THE END OF THE COMPILATION
$4354 THE LIBRARY ROUTINE AT $0947 THAT RESETS THE STACK
$435A RUNTIME IS 4013 BYTES LONG
$4360 THE LIBRARY NORMALLY LOADS AT $0803
$441C THE SLOT AND DRIVE DOS LAST USED: THE BOOT DRIVE
$4366 TWO BELLS FOR THE ERROR MESSAGES
$437E CONTROL-D STARTS EACH DOS COMMAND
$4387 THE LINE NUMBER FILE: PASS 1 WRITES EACH LINE'S NUMBER AND ADDRESS, PASS 2 READS THEM
$439B THE DOS COMMANDS THE PASSES USE
$4434 THE BOOT DRIVE AS ",SN,DN"
$4468 THE DRIVE'S MOTOR-ON SWITCH, $C089 + SLOT*16
$4480 DOS'S OUTPUT STATE BYTE, $AA52
$4516 ASSUME THE FILES ARE ON THE BOOT DRIVE
$4535 THE ANSWER
$4538 QUESTION 2: THE SOURCE FILE
$453E CHECK THE ANSWER (A LINE STARTING WITH CONTROL-D IS A DOS COMMAND)
$4549 AN EMPTY ANSWER IS NOT A FILE NAME
$4560 SPLIT IT INTO NAME AND SLOT/DRIVE
$456B THE SOURCE FILE
$4577 QUESTION 1: THE SOURCE FILE'S EXISTENCE
$457D APPEND FAILS WITH FILE NOT FOUND IF THE FILE DOES NOT EXIST
$45A7 CLOSE IT AGAIN
$45B8 A NAME LONG ENOUGH TO LEAVE ROOM FOR .OBJ
$45F1 ON THE SOURCE FILE'S DRIVE
$4639 A DRIVE OTHER THAN THE BOOT DRIVE IS SHOWN
$4662 QUESTION 3: THE OBJECT FILE
$4673 NOTHING TYPED: THE DEFAULT
$46F1 THE DEFAULT LAYOUT: THE LIBRARY AT $0803, THE PROGRAM RIGHT AFTER IT, THE VARIABLES AFTER THE PROGRAM
$47A0 NOTHING TYPED: THE DEFAULT ADDRESS
$47BA QUESTION 2 FOR THE ADDRESS CHECK: THE LIBRARY
$47CB THE LIBRARY ADDRESS
$4852 NOTHING TYPED: THE PROGRAM FOLLOWS THE LIBRARY
$486F HGR1: THE PROGRAM STARTS AT $4000, ABOVE HIGH-RESOLUTION PAGE 1
$4893 HGR2: AT $6000, ABOVE PAGE 2
$48B7 QUESTION 1 FOR THE ADDRESS CHECK: THE PROGRAM
$48C8 THE PROGRAM ADDRESS
$4928 NOTHING TYPED: THE VARIABLES FOLLOW THE PROGRAM (STORED AS -32767)
$4942 QUESTION 3 FOR THE ADDRESS CHECK: THE VARIABLES
$4953 THE VARIABLES ADDRESS
$495F THE ADDRESSES ARE SHOWN AS THEY ARE, NOT IN THE STORED FORM
$4A6C NO: ASK FOR THE ADDRESSES AGAIN
$4AC5 THE DEFAULT OPTIONS: LISTING, PAUSE, INTEGER ARITHMETIC AND INTEGER CONSTANTS ON, RESUME/DEBUG OFF
$4B40 YES OR NOTHING TYPED: 1; NO: 0
$4C8A ONLY YES TURNS IT ON
$4C96 THE CALL TABLE, 136 ENTRIES (INDEX 0 FIRST)
$4F8F THE DOS PATCH DATA COMES FIRST ...
$4F92 ... 18 VALUES, SKIPPED
$4FAE 136 ENTRIES
$4FBF A ROM ADDRESS: STORED AS ADDRESS-32767
$4FDF A LIBRARY ROUTINE: ITS OFFSET PLUS THE LIBRARY ADDRESS
$5002 17 OPERATORS: ( ) NOT + - * / ^ AND OR > = < AND THE TWO-CHARACTER RELATIONS (235-237), THEN NEGATION (239)
$509A 51 VALUES
$50CB THE MACHINE CODE, 89 BYTES FOR $0377-$03CF: $0377 USR STORES THE FLOATING POINT ACCUMULATOR, ROUNDED, AS 5 PACKED BYTES AT $0371; $037E READS A BYTE (RDKEY, WHICH DOS FEEDS FROM THE OPEN FILE) INTO $0376; $0387 PRINTS THE BYTE IN $0376 (COUT, WHICH DOS SENDS TO THE OPEN FILE); $038D LISTS THE TOKENIZED LINE AT $0280, SPELLING EACH TOKEN FROM THE ROM'S KEYWORD TABLE
$5219 887 TO 975 = $0377 TO $03CF
$5241 THE USR VECTOR AT $0A: JMP $0377
$5265 32 CHAINS EACH FOR VARIABLES, CONSTANTS AND LINE NUMBERS
$5277 CHAIN HEADS 1-4 ARE FN SYMBOLS, 5-8 TEMPORARIES, THEN VARIABLES FROM 9, CONSTANTS AND LINE NUMBERS
$5298 THE ENTRY POINTS OF THE MACHINE CODE AND ITS DATA CELLS
$52BC ALL CHAINS EMPTY
$52E1 A ONE-BYTE BINARY FILE MAKES SURE THE OBJECT FILE EXISTS (AND IS A BINARY FILE)
$5319 OPEN, DELETE AND OPEN AGAIN: AN EMPTY LINE NUMBER FILE
$5358 POSITION IT AT ITS START
$5376 CLOSE ALL FILES
$53AC STRING STORAGE IS SET UP SO THAT THE COMMON STRINGS SURVIVE THE CHAIN TO PASS 1
$53E8 ACCEPTED UNLESS FOUND OTHERWISE
$5456 ANYTHING ELSE: THE BELL, AND THE QUESTION IS ASKED AGAIN
$5463 THE ROM'S INPUT LINE ROUTINE (INLIN, $D52C) READS INTO THE BUFFER AT $0200
$5475 CONTROL-C FIRST STOPS THE PROGRAM
$548C COLLECT CHARACTERS UP TO THE ZERO AT THE END OF THE LINE
$54C8 LOOK FOR A COMMA
$54DC NO COMMA: THE WHOLE LINE IS THE NAME, ON THE BOOT DRIVE
$5517 A NAME CANNOT BE EMPTY
$5549 SKIP LEADING SPACES; A NAME OF SPACES ONLY IS ILLEGAL
$5598 {LS} SERVES HERE AS SCRATCH (IT IS SET TO ITS REAL VALUE LATER): THE LAST CHARACTER THAT IS NOT A SPACE
$55DE DOS USES AT MOST 30 CHARACTERS
$55FE NO SLOT OR DRIVE GIVEN: DONE
$5606 THE SLOT AND DRIVE PART MAY HAVE AT MOST 20 CHARACTERS
$5632 FIND S AND D, EACH RIGHT AFTER A COMMA, AND THEIR NUMBERS
$56F2 A MISSING SLOT OR DRIVE IS THE BOOT DRIVE'S
$5754 A FILE ON ANOTHER SLOT OR DRIVE: THE BOOT DRIVE'S MOTOR NEED NOT BE KEPT RUNNING
$57B7 SKIP LEADING SPACES
$57FC VAL OF A BAD NUMBER GIVES AN ERROR, CAUGHT AT 3420
$580A TURN ONERR OFF AGAIN (ERRFLG, $D8)
$5819 HEXADECIMAL: DIGITS 0-9 AND A-F; SPACES ARE SKIPPED
$5930 ANY OTHER CHARACTER: NOT AN ADDRESS
$5938 49151 = $BFFF, THE TOP OF MEMORY BELOW THE I/O AREA
$5996 BACK TO THE QUESTION: 1 PROGRAM, 2 LIBRARY, 3 VARIABLES
$59A3 AN ERROR IN VAL: ONERR OFF, AND RESET THE STACK
$59BE A DOS COMMAND: RUN IT, THEN ASK AGAIN ({BD} = 1)
$59F5 A DOS ERROR IS CAUGHT AT 3530
$5A1E ERROR CODE 6 (ERRNUM, $DE) IS FILE NOT FOUND
$5A82 RESET THE STACK AFTER THE ERROR
$5A99 BACK TO THE QUESTION: 1 SOURCE FILE OPENED, 2 SOURCE FILE ANSWERED, 3 OBJECT FILE ANSWERED
